intro: >
  A spectacular coastal village overlooked by one of England's most iconic castles,
  with miles of sandy beach and some of Northumberland's finest scenery.

overview: >
  Bamburgh is one of those places that feels instantly recognisable. Its huge
  castle dominates the skyline above a sweeping stretch of golden sand, while
  the village itself offers places to eat, drink and explore. Whether you're
  visiting for the castle, the beach, the views or simply a day by the coast,
  Bamburgh is one of Northumberland's essential places to experience.

getting_there: >
  Bamburgh is on the Northumberland coast, around 15 minutes from Alnwick by car.
  The nearest railway station is at Chathill.

best_time: >
  Early morning and late afternoon are particularly good for quieter walks,
  softer light and fewer visitors.

parking: >
  Several car parks are available in and around the village, with additional
  parking close to the beach.

